\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell A thousand thank yous once again for agreeing to help, old friend. It would seem that the future of Gallopolis is in our hands once more!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell You got a Pepper Tree branch! Take it to Prince Faris in the palace in Gallopolis!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Welcome back, old friend! Well? Did you bring me a branch of the Pepper Tree from the First Forest?<yesno>\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell No!? Oh goodness... Please, <pc>, you must try harder! Our brave desert knights are depending on you!\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Oh, praise the sands! How wonderful! Who would have thought that such tiny berries were packed with such miraculous powers!?\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Eating a few of these will cause the consumer to enter a state of intense focus. Some refer to it as being \lquote pepped up\rquote .\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Of course, a single handful will not go very far when I have an entire army in need of pepping up. An endless supply would be preferable.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Which is why I asked you to bring me the branch! If I could somehow graft this onto one of our local trees, all our problems would be solved!\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell A thousand thank yous once again, <pc>. Perhaps you would like to take one of the pips as a reward?\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Pep pips are said to greatly boost concentration on the battlefield. Our desert knights are sure to find them most useful.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Now that we have some, our next priority must be to secure a continuous supply. I have already contacted some of Erdrea's finest botanists and invited them to Gallopolis in order to assist us in this.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl Prince Faris\cell Of course, I am not expecting our initial efforts to be successful. But even if we require another branch or two from the Pepper Tree, I am sure you will be glad to fetch them for us, will you not, old friend!? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: Cor blimey! Leave it out, will ya? I ain't exactly in the mood for a chinwag right now. I've been worn down by the injustices o' life, see. I just want to lie here till it don't 'urt no more. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: I set sail on a quest to find a legendary crystal lily, but then me boat sank, an' I washed up 'ere wiv nuffink but the clothes on me back.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I ain't got no friends 'ere, no one I can turn to for 'elp... I'm all alone... I might as well just give up... Gah, why did it 'ave to end this way...?\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I must've been born under the unluckiest star in the 'ole o' the 'eavens! I'd be better off dead...\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: (sob) All I ever wanted was a look at a crystal lily... Just one... (sniff) Was that too much to ask...?\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: If only some kind soul would bring me one, I could die 'appy... (sniff) \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell You've been asked to undertake a quest.\par
Will you acquiesce to this request?<yesno>\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: Ha... Yeah, that's about right. There ain't no kind souls in this rotten world. I'll just lie 'ere and wait till it's all over... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: S-Seriously!? ...'Ang on, I know your game\f1\emdash\f0 yer just gettin' me 'opes up so you can dash 'em to the ground again, ain'tcha?\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Well, s'pose I ain't got nuffink to lose by 'opin'. If you find a crystal lily on yer travels, bring it back 'ere, eh?\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I 'ear they only grow far to the north of 'ere, on the 'igh plateaus of Snifl'eim, where the freezin' blizzards blow.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: ...It's too far away, ain't it? Too much of a faff to trudge through all that snow? Fine, forget it, then.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I'll just carry on lyin' 'ere till the last dregs o' me rotten life ebb away. If you do find a crystal lily, then this is where I'll be... Fat chance o' that 'appenin', though... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: Crystal lilies only grow far to the north of 'ere, on the 'igh plateaus of Snifl'eim, where the freezin' blizzards blow.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Pretty long way to go for a flower, ain't it? If you give up 'alfway, I won't blame ya.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I'll just carry on lyin' here till the last dregs o' me rotten life ebb away. If you do find a crystal lily, then this is where I'll be... Fat chance o' that 'appenin', though... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell You found a crystal lily! You should take it back to the crestfallen castaway in Lonalulu! \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: Oh, yer back. You gonna try an' make me believe you went an' got me a crystal lily or somefink? <yesno>\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: Heh heh heh. Didn't think so. I knew I was right not to get me 'opes up. Only thing in me rotten life I ever did get right, mind... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: Y-You did it! This is a crystal lily! An actual crystal lily! I can't believe you actually did a favour for a washed-up, worn-out wreck of a bloke like me!\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Then it is just as I hypothesised\f1\emdash\f0 no predicament, no matter how hopeless it may seem, is truly irremediable!\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Forgive me for deceiving you, but in truth, I am not a castaway. I am currently conducting research into human psychology, with a particular focus on the altruistic instinct.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: When the dark star appeared in the sky and spread its evil aura across Erdrea, I began to question whether compassion would survive the pressures of self-preservation.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: I hoped that it would, but, scientist that I am, I could not rely on hope alone. Hence, I devised this experiment...and you have proved my hypothesis to be true!\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Thank you, my friend. Please, take this as a reward for your kind efforts. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: That you brought the legendary crystal lily to me proves that your heart is pure. I pray that you will stay that way forever more.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: So long as there are people like you in this world, I am sure that love and laughter will return to us in time. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: From dawn to dusk, I devote my time to studying the ancient teachings of Angri-La.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Our temple's rich and storied history goes all the way back to the Age of Heroes. Over the years, we have accumulated quite a collection of fascinating tomes. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell There's an ancient book. <pc> can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Wizard's Canticle \f1\endash\f0  Book I\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell But it's magically sealed, and he can't read it... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell There's an ancient book. <pc> can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Wizard's Canticle \f1\endash\f0  Book II\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell But it's magically sealed, and he can't read it... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell There's an ancient book. <pc> can only just make out the words \lquote Ye Wizard's Canticle \f1\endash\f0  Book III\rquote  on the faded, threadbare cover.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell But it's magically sealed, and he can't read it... \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: \lquote Ye art of sorcery consisteth in ye manipulation of ye magickal energies that courseth through a wizard's veins. This being so, ye magickal might of any given spellcaster is necessarily limited by ye extent of said power.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: \lquote But long years of study have revealed unto me a secret by which ye power that floweth through Erdrea's very soil might be channelled, thereby rendering a magick's power greatly more potent.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: \lquote Yea, 'tis an art only for ye wisest and greatest of wizards. This being so, I have hidden its secrets in three tomes, and hidden these tomes in their turn among ye threefold floors of ye Sniflheimian Royal Library.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: \lquote If I should fail in laying the Dark One low, thou who followest in my footsteps, I prithee\f1\emdash\f0 seek out ye tomes, and pronounce these words before them:\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: \lquote\ldblquote Slumb'ring place of strength untold, break thy bonds! Unlock! Unfold!\rdblquote\rquote\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\par
*: ...Ah, forgive me. I did not notice you there. I am studying the ancient teachings of Angri-La.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: This book was written by Morcant, the great sorcerer who joined the Luminary of Legend in his battle with the Dark One. I discovered it in the temple's storerooms only recently.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: If Lord Robert were to follow Morcant's instructions and learn to channel Erdrea's energies, it would surely benefit you greatly.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: You have been to the Royal Library before, have you not? Will you return there and seek out his secrets? \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell You've been asked to undertake a quest.\par
Will you acquiesce to this request?<yesno>\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: ...As you wish. But remember this\f1\emdash\f0 a moment's inconvenience in the present can spare a lifetime's suffering in the future. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: Good. Then you must journey to Sniflheim, and eastward into the Sn\'e6rfelt where the Royal Library stands. Morcant hid three books there, it seems\f1\emdash\f0 one on each floor of that great repository of wisdom.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: \lquote Slumb'ring place of strength untold, break thy bonds! Unlock! Unfold!\rquote\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: This is the mantra that you must repeat before each one to break its seal. Good luck. Return to me when you have read all three tomes. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: It seems Morcant placed three books on the shelves of the Royal Library, which lies to the east of Sniflheim\f1\emdash\f0 one on each floor of that great repository of knowledge.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: \lquote Slumb'ring place of strength untold, break thy bonds! Unlock! Unfold!\rquote\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell *: This is the mantra that you must repeat before each one to break its seal. Good luck. Return to me when you have read all three tomes. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell You've read all three parts of Ye Wizard's Canticle! Head back to Angri-La and tell the studious disciple standing near the inn what you've learned! \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell There's an ancient book here entitled \lquote Ye Wizard's Canticle \f1\endash\f0  Book I\rquote . This must be the sealed grimoire of Morcant's that the monk at Angri-La told <pc> about.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell He recites the mantra that he learned from the monk, and the spell protecting the book is broken! He opens the cover and begins to read...\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\lquote Hear me, O spirits of ye great realm of Erdrea\f1\emdash\f0 realm of boundless skies, of bottomless seas, of endless plains\f1\emdash\f0 heed my call!\rquote\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell It must be part of the incantation Morcant used to make his magic more powerful. <pc> carefully commits it to memory. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell There's an ancient book here entitled \lquote Ye Wizard's Canticle \f1\endash\f0  Book II\rquote . This must be the sealed grimoire of Morcant's that the monk at Angri-La told <pc> about.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell He recites the mantra that he learned from the monk, and the spell protecting the book is broken! He opens the cover and begins to read...\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\lquote Grant unto me thy power, that I might protect this beauteous world and thy children, its peoples, from ye foul machinations of that most vile and villainous of beasts\f1\emdash\f0 ye Dark One!\rquote\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell It must be part of the incantation Morcant used to make his magic more powerful. <pc> carefully commits it to memory. \cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh581\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell There's an ancient book here entitled \lquote Ye Wizard's Canticle \f1\endash\f0  Book III\rquote . This must be the sealed grimoire of Morcant's that the monk at Angri-La told <pc> about.\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell He recites the mantra that he learned from the monk, and the spell protecting the book is broken! He opens the cover and begins to read...\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
\pard\intbl\cell\lquote Lend me thy might\f1\emdash\f0 fleeting and ephemeral, sublime and blinding! Rain down upon me thy glorious luminance!\rquote\par
\cell\row\trowd\trgaph30\trleft-30\trrh290\trpaddl30\trpaddr30\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\cellx1410\cellx10343 
